"""
ant-mcp — Anthive MCP Server

Exposes Anthive single-cell RNA-seq data as MCP tools so any LLM session
(Claude Code, Claude Desktop, Cursor, …) can query datasets and generate
plots via natural language.

The MCP server wraps the ant-serve REST API — it never touches DuckDB
directly, so it can run on any machine that can reach the API URL.

Usage (local):
    ant-mcp --api-url http://localhost:8080

Usage (remote HTTP server, proxied through nginx):
    ant-mcp --api-url http://localhost:8080 --port 8090

Authentication: every signed-in user gets a personal link from the web UI
(account menu, "MCP link"), of the form

    https://anthive.example.org/mcp/u/amcp_<id>_<mac>

Clients that support headers can instead send the token to /mcp as
``Authorization: Bearer amcp_<id>_<mac>``. Tokens are verified against
ant-serve (/internal/mcp/verify); tool calls then run with that user's
identity, and admin-only tools are hidden from non-admins.
See doc/MCP_LINKS.md.
"""

